  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Goalkeeper – come out when the attacker is under pressure",
  "description": "Three against three with keepers on a pitch about 20 metres wide and 30 metres long, with small goals or cone goals. Outfield players may touch the ball at most twice in a row. So the player on the ball is often short of time: a defender is chasing them, the first touch is too heavy, or the ball bounces.\n\nThe keeper reads those moments and acts at once: come all the way out and take the ball before the attacker can shoot, or go down and block with the whole body. The keepers may also join the attack as an extra player. To make them dare, goals only count from inside about ten metres from goal – mark the line with cones.\n\nPlay periods of four minutes. Variation: goals only count from low shots. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Read the touch: when the ball runs away from the attacker, that is your chance – go at once."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Once you have decided, go all the way and at full speed."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "If you can’t get all the way: go down wide towards the ball, hands first."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "If you joined the attack: sprint back as soon as the ball is lost."
    }
  ],
